      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Testicular tumors are the most common solid tumors in young adult males. Patients with testicular tumor often present with painless scrotal mass. Rarely, symptoms are related to metastases. We describe the case of a patient presenting with abdominal pain due to retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy. We describe the magnetic resonance imaging findings of lumbar spine osseous metastasis."},
